From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: add Qualcomm gen1 port backend

Unmodified aggregate of patches 01, 03, 04, 05, 06, 08 from David Heidelberg's
2026-09-26 RFC "Qualcomm Type-C support for 1st generation":
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260926-typec-v1-0-31adc19f32c6@ixit.cz/
https://patchew.org/linux/20260926-typec-v1-0-31adc19f32c6@ixit.cz/

The selected patches add the gen1 shared Qualcomm TCPM backend, its binding,
and a disabled PMI8998 controller node. Phone board DTS changes are omitted.
The original RFC covers externally powered docks and has no VBUS source
provider; the following local patch supplies mici's dedicated source path.

Applied to Linux c03c1a14507dfaf8b856c2608f9ac216021fc222 (v7.3).
Original mbox SHA256:
e35d6beaff5089f72ab7c1829a9d295af2f7e35b224120c1aeb46e3581b1969b

